- COVID-19 Global Impact Dashboard
- A data analytics project built to explore global COVID-19 trends, regional wave trajectories, and population-normalized impacts using Python and Power BI.
1. Assumptions:
- Missing Daily Counts: Days with missing new_cases or new_deaths were filled with 0, assuming no new cases or deaths were reported on those specific days.
- Separation of Aggregates: Global aggregates (like 'World') were kept in a separate table/view so they don't distort individual country comparisons when plotting
  totals.
- Case Fatality Rate (CFR): Calculated as ("Total Deaths" /"Total Cases" )×100. Undefined values (where total cases equal zero) were handled by setting CFR to zero.

2. Project Overview
This project processes publicly available COVID-19 time-series data from Our World in Data (OWID). It focuses on cleaning real-world dataset anomalies, removing reporting noise, deriving key epidemiological metrics (Case Fatality Rate), and visualizing insights in an interactive Power BI dashboard.


3. Tools & Technologies Used
-Python (Pandas):Data cleaning, missing value imputation, and feature engineering.
-Microsoft Power BI:Interactive visualization, slicers, and dashboard layouts.
-Excel / CSV: Raw data storage and export format.

