5. Data Cleaning Pipeline-
- The raw dataset was transformed using Python (data_cleaning.py) following these steps:
	- Handling Missing Values: Filled null daily counts (new_cases, new_deaths) with 0.
	- Filtering Aggregates: Excluded aggregate regional records (e.g., World, Europe, High income) to ensure clean country-to-country comparisons.
	- Metric Calculation: Calculated the Case Fatality Rate (CFR) directly:
  - "CFR (%)"=("Total Deaths" /"Total Cases" )×100
	Export: Outputted the refined dataset as cleaned_covid_data.csv.
6. Dashboard Key Features-
	- Dropdown Filters: Filter by country (location) and date range without vertical scrolling.
	- KPI Overview Cards: Total Cases, Total Deaths, and Average Case Fatality Rate at a glance.
	- Top 10 Impacted Countries: Horizontal bar chart filtered using Top N rules to display population-normalized metrics (total_cases_per_million).
	- Wave Progression: Line chart plotting smoothed daily counts over time to show pandemic wave trajectories.
7. Key Insights-
	- Population Normalization Matters: Raw case counts favor larger nations; evaluating cases per million reveals the true relative impact density across countries.
	- Smooth Trends vs. Daily Noise: 7-day smoothing eliminates artificial weekend reporting drops to show true pandemic progression.
	- Regional Mortality Variations: Case Fatality Rates vary significantly due to differences in testing coverage, age demographics, and local healthcare capacity.






















